    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1835 a covered bridge spanned the Delaware River to Raven Rock, New Jersey, but one span was lost in the 1903 flood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumberville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village hosted Lock #12 of the Delaware Canal, a set of locks that moved barges between Easton and Bristol.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumberville%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Black Bass Hotel, built in the early 1740s, later became known as the Rising Sun and other taverns over the years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
